import 'package:drift/drift.dart';

/// Complete canonical master-data seed for offline terminal initialization.
///
/// Implements Objective 3: Complete Offline Canonical Seed.
/// A brand-new offline terminal starts with the full canonical catalog
/// required for cashier operations without depending on an initial remote sync.
///
/// All records use deterministic, static UUIDs identical to Supabase dev/prod baselines.
/// All statements use `INSERT OR IGNORE` for idempotency across restarts.
/// Zero `sync_operations` outbox records are generated by this seed.
///
/// IMPORTANT: This seed is strictly OPT-IN. It is NOT executed on normal
/// startup; a fresh install starts with an empty local database and master
/// data is created by the user through the app (and pushed via the normal
/// sync/outbox flow). Enable explicitly for development/tests with:
/// `flutter run --dart-define=ENABLE_CANONICAL_SEED=true`
/// (independent of `ENABLE_DEV_TEST_DATA`).
class SeedData {
  /// Last sequence emitted by the canonical remote master-data baseline.
  ///
  /// The baseline contains 35 sync changes: aggregate service and storage
  /// changes include their junction rows. A canonical local database starts
  /// at this cursor so it does not replay its own bootstrap history.
  static const int canonicalBaselineSequence = 35;

  /// Compile-time opt-in flag for canonical seeding. Defaults to `false`.
  static const bool isEnabled = bool.fromEnvironment(
    'ENABLE_CANONICAL_SEED',
    defaultValue: false,
  );

